{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220678-the-crit-train-doesn-t-stop","id":1220678,"title":"The crit train doesn't stop","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-20T18:48:23-07:00","id":1220678,"title":"The crit train doesn't stop","content":"So I'm running a game with a Mind mage and two Fate mages. The Mind mage's favorite spells are Augment Mind and Enhance Skill. The Fate mages both have Exceptional Luck as a rote. <br /> <br /> As a result I'm regularly seeing mental and social rolls with 10 or more successes. Including a roll that got 12 successes while using the Inspired Condition, meaning that it got four times over the necessary amount for an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> Because of this, I end up handing out positive conditions like candy and thus beats are flowing at a prodigious rate.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt doesn't help that the default Condition, Inspired, for exceptionally succeeding has the result of making a subsequent roll likely to exceptionally succeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T20:18:07-07:00","id":1220698,"title":"","content":"This sounds to me like the game working as intended. Your players are using their powers effectively and efficiently and engaging deep/y with the game and thus they're earning Beats (and thus, Experience) at a prodigious rate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T20:19:05-07:00","id":1220699,"title":"","content":"Thank you for sharing your experience? I'm not sure if this is a critique or observation of play thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T20:33:28-07:00","id":1220702,"title":"","content":"I believe what the OP couldn't quite put into words is: he's having a hard time challenging his players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T20:42:54-07:00","id":1220704,"title":"","content":"Hmm... well dice rolls are meant to be for things that the character has an actual chance at failing IC, or promise something interesting dramatic OOC should it fail. By this point it\u2019s neither, so you could just say the mages auto-succeed at trivial things.<br /> <br /> This also means no excessive exceptional successes, something that may be puzzling since if the characters are so good at things to the point they literally can\u2019t fail, then it seems that exceptional successes should also always follow suit. You can get around this by saying that exceptional successes work by pushing over each characters\u2019 relative standards. That is, they only get exceptionals when doing things that matter, not every time they do stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T20:48:02-07:00","id":1220707,"title":"","content":"When resolving Inspired, I don't allow the resulting exceptional success to yield a Condition to the same player that had Inspired - but I do let them bring a Condition into play on another character, such as adding a negative Condition to the target of the action. It's a house rule, obviously, and doesn't fully address this 'problem' but I've found that it helps people be more creative when they get exceptionals and keeps things interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T21:35:17-07:00","id":1220718,"title":"","content":"Beat gain from Conditions is relatively easily considered and capped in many situations.<br /> <br /> Remember those Conditions gained from spells as an inherent part of the spell (as opposed to generated by an Exceptional Success in spellcasting) don't offer a Beat on resolutions.<br /> And there is a cap on 1 Arcane and 1 mundane Beat per Scene, derived from Conditions.<br /> An easy way to avoid ludicrous gains, is to expand the duration of each scene.<br /> <br /> If it's causing a problem in your game, and you don't want it to continue, talk to your players about it.<br /> Exceptional Luck is a stupidly powerful spell, especially when taken as a Rote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T22:28:28-07:00","id":1220726,"title":"","content":"As 21C Hermit said before you're only supposed to roll when it's dramatically appropriate aka. when there is risk of failure and consequenced for that failure. If they keep doing it that way and you feel they[re advancing too fast (I believe this is the source of your complaint). But best talk with the players about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T23:41:06-07:00","id":1220743,"title":"","content":"Expanding on what others have said:<br /> <br /> <br /> You get beat generating conditions when you get an Exceptional Success because you <i>learn</i> from the experience, if the task is so trivial to you that you don't learn anything then you don't learn anything no matter how well you do. A third grader suddenly &quot;getting&quot; basic multiplication might be Inspired by how well they did on a homework (an exceptional success), a college math major shouldn't even be rolling because they can't fail and can't exceptionally succeed: perfect success is assumed and is therefore just a &quot;normal&quot; success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T10:08:54-07:00","id":1220871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220678-the-crit-train-doesn-t-stop?p=1220704#post1220704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... well dice rolls are meant to be for things that the character has an actual chance at failing IC, or promise something interesting dramatic OOC should it fail. By this point it\u2019s neither, so you could just say the mages auto-succeed at trivial things.<br /> <br /> This also means no excessive exceptional successes, something that may be puzzling since if the characters are so good at things to the point they literally can\u2019t fail, then it seems that exceptional successes should also always follow suit. You can get around this by saying that exceptional successes work by pushing over each characters\u2019 relative standards. That is, they only get exceptionals when doing things that matter, not every time they do stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>So no: <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> &quot;You've have exceptionally succeeded at putting on your shoes this morning! Much Inspired!&quot;<br /> <img src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/378800000822867536/3f5a00acf72df93528b6bb7cd0a4fd0c_400x400.jpeg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T10:12:10-07:00","id":1220873,"title":"","content":"To back up what everyone else is saying - if they've stacked the deck enough that success is certain, why bother rolling? Use Down and Dirty Spellcasting, if you still feel the urge to roll dice.<br /> <br /> Alternatively - your players have shown you exactly how to break the system and how annoying it can be. What's good for them is good for Antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T17:34:05-07:00","id":1221004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lareath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220678-the-crit-train-doesn-t-stop#post1220678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a result I'm regularly seeing mental and social rolls with 10 or more successes. Including a roll that got 12 successes while using the Inspired Condition, meaning that it got four times over the necessary amount for an exceptional success.</div> </div> </div> </div>An important question: are these chains of Inspiration <i>actually linked</i>? That is to say, are you enforced the connection between what earned the Inspired Condition and what they're discharging it on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T17:44:06-07:00","id":1221006,"title":"","content":"In the situation described in the OP, inspired is something of a red herring anyway.<br /> <br /> Getting an exceptional success on 3 instead of 5 hardly matters when you're routinely rolling 10+","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T19:51:25-07:00","id":1221041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220678-the-crit-train-doesn-t-stop?p=1220704#post1220704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... well dice rolls are meant to be for things that the character has an actual chance at failing IC, or promise something interesting dramatic OOC should it fail. By this point it\u2019s neither, so you could just say the mages auto-succeed at trivial things.<br /> <br /> This also means no excessive exceptional successes, something that may be puzzling since if the characters are so good at things to the point they literally can\u2019t fail, then it seems that exceptional successes should also always follow suit. You can get around this by saying that exceptional successes work by pushing over each characters\u2019 relative standards. That is, they only get exceptionals when doing things that matter, not every time they do stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I try to only have them roll in circumstances where failure is meaningful. It's when they do things like &quot;try to get help from that nominally allied group of shady Guardians we accidentally gave disasterously bad information to, researching something the shady Guardians are secretly covering up&quot; that I end up flabbergasted at social crit chains<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220678-the-crit-train-doesn-t-stop?p=1220707#post1220707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When resolving Inspired, I don't allow the resulting exceptional success to yield a Condition to the same player that had Inspired - but I do let them bring a Condition into play on another character, such as adding a negative Condition to the target of the action. It's a house rule, obviously, and doesn't fully address this 'problem' but I've found that it helps people be more creative when they get exceptionals and keeps things interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this house rule.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220678-the-crit-train-doesn-t-stop?p=1220873#post1220873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To back up what everyone else is saying - if they've stacked the deck enough that success is certain, why bother rolling? Use Down and Dirty Spellcasting, if you still feel the urge to roll dice.<br /> <br /> Alternatively - your players have shown you exactly how to break the system and how annoying it can be. What's good for them is good for Antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well obviously. It's just rather hard to represent utterly inhuman persuasiveness without taking away player agency to an unacceptable degree. I'm contemplating an Exalted style &quot;you may spend willpower and risk a breaking point to auto-resist&quot;. <br /> <br /> That said, it is funny how utterly terrified the players are of an nice little old lady that does patriotic charity bake-sales and runs a soup kitchen. She's done absolutely nothing to them except have a nice, genuinely friendly chat. It's probably because it was only during the &quot;shake hands and introduce yourself&quot; part of the conversation that they realized they were shaking hands with the most powerful Seer in the city, an Uncrowned King with the Prelacy of Unity<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220678-the-crit-train-doesn-t-stop?p=1221004#post1221004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An important question: are these chains of Inspiration <i>actually linked</i>? That is to say, are you enforced the connection between what earned the Inspired Condition and what they're discharging it on?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220678-the-crit-train-doesn-t-stop?p=1221006#post1221006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the situation described in the OP, inspired is something of a red herring anyway.<br /> <br /> Getting an exceptional success on 3 instead of 5 hardly matters when you're routinely rolling 10+</div> </div> </div> </div>It's what potentially keeps the crit chain going even when they deal with something they AREN'T prepared and buffed for. Or when they roll poorly despite lots of dice with 8-again","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T19:56:12-07:00","id":1221047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lareath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220678-the-crit-train-doesn-t-stop?p=1221041#post1221041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's what potentially keeps the crit chain going even when they deal with something they AREN'T prepared and buffed for. Or when they roll poorly despite lots of dice with 8-again</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you assign Conditions for exceptional successes yourself, or allow the players to decide what they want, or a mix of both?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T20:50:53-07:00","id":1221061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220678-the-crit-train-doesn-t-stop?p=1221047#post1221047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you assign Conditions for exceptional successes yourself, or allow the players to decide what they want, or a mix of both?</div> </div> </div> </div>A mix of both, depending on circumstances and how inspired I'm feeling","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T22:51:42-07:00","id":1221081,"title":"","content":"Alright... I could excuse the &quot;crit train&quot; as you're calling it, if the victims of it weren't also mages. Guardians of the Veil no less. Don't they have mental defenses? a policy to meet whomever they meet in a special warded place that snuffs out such spells? Isn't their impression of the characters under that circumstance abysmal? Couldn't there be someone versed in Fate/Time enough to determine that giving these guys a hand would blow up in their face, regardless of how charming they are? That alone would make social maneuvering attempts (and I hope you're using that system for these scenarios), not merely difficult, but impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T19:15:51-07:00","id":1221351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220678-the-crit-train-doesn-t-stop?p=1221081#post1221081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright... I could excuse the &quot;crit train&quot; as you're calling it, if the victims of it weren't also mages. Guardians of the Veil no less. Don't they have mental defenses? a policy to meet whomever they meet in a special warded place that snuffs out such spells? Isn't their impression of the characters under that circumstance abysmal? Couldn't there be someone versed in Fate/Time enough to determine that giving these guys a hand would blow up in their face, regardless of how charming they are? That alone would make social maneuveriang attempts (and I hope you're using that system for these scenarios), not merely difficult, but impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was helpful. And after further thought, I've decided the simplest answer that fits what already happened is that they have a strict &quot;after action review&quot; policy for plotting their next course of action. And also that possibly the person the player talked to was just a stand-in cut-away sleepwalker retainer, and not the real Protagonist*.<br /> <br /> *The GotV group is The Theater with members being The Antagonist, The Protagonist, The Stagehand, The Conductor, and The Director. Among other things they specialize in dreamsculpting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T22:16:31-07:00","id":1221385,"title":"","content":"The proverbial <a href=\"http://tolkiengateway.net/wiki/The_Voice_of_Saruman\" target=\"_blank\">Voice of Saruman</a> is scarily real in a Mage setting, so yeah, you have to account for it setting wise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}